That's an interesting question, and one I can't answer (I'm not about to try
and check the code until I get my own computer up and running).  I can,
however,
tell you why super enchanted Magicbanes don't work to well.  The chance of 
getting the special effects of Magicbane is directly related to the
weapon's level
of enchantment.  That is, the more enchanted it is, the less chance
you'll have of
purging your target.  Which leads to an interesting question:  would a negative
enchanted Magicbane do even better at purging monsters?


